      "title": "Early Dynastic Egypt",
      "periodLabel": "3000 BCE context",
      "summary": "A unified Egyptian monarchy stood along the Nile. Royal authority connected Upper and Lower Egypt; this early state should not be read as the modern country.",
      "institutions": [
        "Kingship linked Upper and Lower Egypt.",
        "Memphis, between the two regions, became an important royal center; Abydos remained a royal burial place."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "The Early Dynastic period followed unification around 3100 BCE; its chronology is approximate."
      ],
