      "title": "Middle Kingdom Egypt",
      "periodLabel": "2000 BCE context",
      "summary": "Egypt was reunited under the Theban royal house after an era of regional rule. Kingship again connected the Nile valley, with royal and regional centers participating in government and religious life.",
      "institutions": [
        "Mentuhotep II’s reunification began the Middle Kingdom around 2030 BCE.",
        "The king combined political and religious authority; regional elites and temples were part of the kingdom’s organization."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "The reunification of Upper and Lower Egypt preceded this observation; later Dynasty 12 reforms should not be projected back into 2000 BCE."
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
