      "title": "New Kingdom Egypt",
      "periodLabel": "1500 BCE context",
      "summary": "The Eighteenth Dynasty ruled a reunited Egyptian kingdom. The royal court and the cult of Amun at Thebes supported an expanding state with military interests beyond the Nile valley.",
      "institutions": [
        "Pharaonic kingship combined government, military leadership and patronage of the gods.",
        "Thebes was a major religious center; royal patronage expanded the temple of Amun at Karnak."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "Ahmose I’s defeat of the Hyksos and reunification of Egypt inaugurated the New Kingdom around 1550 BCE."
      ],
      "sources": [
