      "title": "Ptolemaic Kingdom",
      "periodLabel": "200–100 BCE observations",
      "summary": "A dynasty of Macedonian origin ruled Egypt from Alexandria. The court sustained Egyptian kingship and religious institutions while Greek communities and cultural institutions became prominent.",
      "institutions": [
        "The Ptolemies ruled as a royal dynasty; Alexandria served as their capital.",
        "Egyptian and Greek religious traditions and communities coexisted within the kingdom."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "This kingdom emerged after Alexander’s conquest and the division of his empire; it was distinct from both earlier pharaonic dynasties and later Roman provincial government."
      ],
