      "title": "Roman Empire",
      "periodLabel": "1 BCE · 100 CE · 200 CE observations",
      "summary": "Imperial government linked Rome and its provinces across the Mediterranean. Emperors held dominant power alongside a continuing Senate, officials, provincial administrations and local urban elites.",
